ld just be like once upon a  time bass hung out with us and then she  went to the cool kids table  the end and like that would be it there  really wouldn't be a whole lot more you  know more to give us than that but we  didn't get that and again it's not the  end of the world i don't think it takes  away from the episode i thought it was  fun but it was a fun cool episode i do  like the tension that's going on between  layla and mark spector um i think at the  end of the day the reality of the  situation is going to come out i mean i  think that that tension that's being  built up there is would resonate more  with like non-comic book readers or  people who are unfamiliar with the  history of moon knight and kind of  piecing that stuff together on their own  instead of referencing the source  material if you read the comics like you  know that like layla is a stand-in for  marlene and that layla's father being  like the architect uh i'm sorry the  archaeologist was likely killed by raw  bushmen whether we'll see royal bushman  i don't know i think if we end up seeing  him it'll be as like the very tail end  of the last episode and it's like to be  continued in moon knight season two  right like the guy who like [ __ ] over  mark spector and left him for dead like  that sounds like something they would do  that they would kind of make rob bushman  the main villain for for season two and  we would get more of that story there uh  but the reality is assuming they go with  the original comic book origin for mark  spector that he was basically a  mercenary that was along for the ride  with marlene and her father and then  raul buschmann and those guys and then  ultimately raul bushman just shot  everybody up except for marlene left him  for dead left mark spector for dead and  then of course mark spectre ended up  becoming the avatar of conscious on  earth when his body was taken to the  base of konchu's statue so again it's  just one of those things where they may  swit